        {
          "heading": "Vowels",
          "body": "Finnish has eight vowels. Keep them pure — don't glide them into diphthongs like English does.",
          "table": {
            "headers": [
              "Vowel",
              "Sounds like",
              "Example"
            ],
            "rows": [
              [
                "a",
                "a in 'father' (but short)",
                "kala — fish"
              ],
              [
                "e",
                "e in 'pet'",
                "mene — go"
              ],
              [
                "i",
                "i in 'machine' (short)",
                "tie — road"
              ],
              [
                "o",
                "o in 'hot' with rounded lips",
                "talo — house"
              ],
              [
                "u",
                "oo in 'book'",
                "kuu — moon"
              ],
              [
                "y",
                "German ü / French u: say 'ee' with rounded lips",
                "yksi — one"
              ],
              [
                "ä",
                "a in 'cat'",
                "äiti — mother"
              ],
              [
                "ö",
                "German ö / 'ur' in 'fur' without the r",
                "yö — night"
              ]
            ]
          },
          "tip": "ä and a are different letters, not accents: **sää** (weather) vs **saa** (gets), **pää** (head) vs **paa**. The same goes for ö/o and y/u."
        },
        {
          "heading": "Consonants to watch",
          "bullets": [
            "**r** is always rolled (trilled), even at the end of a word: *kirja*, *tytär*.",
            "**h** is always pronounced, also before a consonant: *kahvi*, *lähteä*, *tehdä*.",
            "**j** sounds like English y: *joulu* ≈ 'youlu', *jäätelö*.",
            "**k, p, t** are unaspirated — softer than in English, no puff of air.",
            "**ng** is a long 'ng' as in 'singer' (never 'finger'): *kengät*, *Helsingissä*.",
            "**nk** is pronounced ŋk as in 'bank': *Helsinki*, *pankki*.",
            "**s** is always a sharp s (never z): *vesi*, *Suomi*."
          ]
        },
        {
          "heading": "Spelling letter by letter",
          "body": "When you spell a name on the phone, say the letter names from the table above. Useful phrases: **Miten se kirjoitetaan?** (How is it written?) — **Voitko tavata sen?** (Can you spell it?).",
          "examples": [
            {
              "fi": "Mikä sinun nimesi on? — Gavin. G-A-V-I-N.",
              "en": "What's your name? — Gavin. gee-aa-vee-ii-än."
            }
          ]
        }
